namespace pdg { /**
\fn pdg::Animated::moveBy(Offset value, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Move by an offset.

Adds the offset to the location. The overload without duration applies immediately. A timed request replaces programmed movement. With andThen(), the relative target is resolved when the operation starts. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param value Relative offset in the container coordinate system.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see moveTo(), setLocation(), andThen()
*/

/**
\fn pdg::Animated::moveBy(number x, number y, number durationSeconds, int easing)
\brief Move by an offset.

Adds the offset to the location. The overload without duration applies immediately. A timed request replaces programmed movement. With andThen(), the relative target is resolved when the operation starts. Durations are explicit floating-point seconds. Zero applies immediately; a request after wait() or andThen() must have positive duration.

\param x Relative offset in the container coordinate system.
\param y Relative offset in the container coordinate system.
\param durationSeconds Finite nonnegative duration in seconds.
\param easing Integer easing constant; elapsed time and duration use seconds.

\return This object, for chaining.

\see moveTo(), setLocation(), andThen()
*/
 }
